        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Moscow</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">1147 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">First documented in 1147, as a meeting place of Yuri Dolgorukiy and Sviatoslav Olgovich. Its first prince was Daniel, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>, who received it as hereditary land in 1263.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On the banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moskva-river">Moskva River</a> on the East European Plain in Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, in the present-day Russian Federation.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Kremlin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-square">Red Square</a>; the rise of Muscovy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-iii">Ivan III</a>; the doctrine of Moscow as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-rome">Third Rome</a>; the burning of the city by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-tatars">Crimean Tatars</a> in 1571; the fire of 1812; capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>; the Moscow Metro; the Battle of Moscow</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Moscow is the capital and largest city of the Russian Federation and is governed as a federal city.</span></div>
